{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/5400-alternate-virtues-rule","id":5400,"title":"Alternate Virtues Rule:","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T14:05:53-08:00","id":5400,"title":"Alternate Virtues Rule:","content":"I am of the opinion that virtues in core Scion are somewhat silly. Trying to define every character who comes from a particular pantheon using the same four single words, in what are effectively various font sizes, seems like it does not help to create truly interesting, iconic characters. However, the idea of being able to draw on particular aspects of a character's personality to enhance actions in line with it does have merit in a mechanical, as well as a roleplay sense.<br /> <br /> To that end, I have made an attempt to use the aspect rules of the FATE system in conjunction with Scion's systems, to create a more versatile, and hopefully more interesting system. I am posting the exact text I have put in a houserules document for a campaign I'm starting soon, and I am looking for feedback both on content and on wording.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Instead of virtues, you must have four aspects that describe your character\u2019s personality. Each should be written in a way that it can be either helpful or detrimental to the character. You may channel each aspect a number of times equal to your legend per story, to gain bonus dice equal to your legend on an action to which the aspect is applicable. You may, or the Storyteller may, choose to \u201ccompel\u201d an aspect. When an aspect is compelled to get your character to take an action in line with one of their aspects, but otherwise detrimental, you have two options. First, you may recharge a use of channeling your aspects, and take the action in question. Second, you may spend a use of channeling in order to not have to take that action.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T15:02:19-08:00","id":5451,"title":"","content":"I don't really agree with that, virtues as written aren't really personality traits, they are more like the values of you pantheon infused by the ichor of your parents, that is why mortals don't have virtues, your personality is your nature. Now about the system you made it's good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/883-volv","name":"VolV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}